#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cctop: a live list of running Claude Code sessions, meant for a pinned Warp tab.

  cctop                 interactive view (fzf), refreshes every few seconds
  cctop list            one snapshot, tab-separated (what the view renders)
  cctop preview <id>    details for one session
  cctop jump <id>       focus the session's Warp tab (via its warp://session focus link)
  cctop close <id>      stop a session after confirmation
  cctop attach <id>     attach to a background session
  cctop open-pr <id>    open the session's linked PR in the browser
  cctop code <id>       open the session's directory in VS Code
  cctop diff <id>       page through the session's changes against the default branch
  cctop reopen <session-id> <dir> <title>   resume a session in a new Warp tab

Sessions come from `claude agents --json`; titles, branch, PR and last messages from each
session's transcript tail. PR states are fetched with `gh` in the background and cached.

Requires macOS, Warp, Python 3.8+, fzf 0.71+ and the Claude Code CLI; `gh`, VS Code's `code` and
diff-so-fancy are optional. Parts of it read Claude Code and Warp files that aren't documented
interfaces, so an update to either can break things.
"""
